00:11:58,700 --> 00:11:59,700
Right!

286
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:15,700
Come to think of it, I guess he was the setter.

287
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,700
Focus on the next one, guys!

288
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:18,700
Right!

289
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:20,700
Give us a good serve!

290
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:21,700
Good serve!

291
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:24,700
Ah!

292
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:25,700
Daiji!

293
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:26,700
Crap!

294
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,700
Too short!

295
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:28,700
Good, it's off course.

296
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:33,700
What?!

297
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:37,700
A fast attack right there!

298
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:39,700
How'd they pull that out of their ass?!

299
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,700
That was incredible, Hinata!

300
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:44,700
I'm kinda having a hard time believing that!

301
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:45,700
That was amazing!

302
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:52,700
I know I sound salty, but their setter is ticking me off.

303
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:54,700
Show them what you got, Tanaka!

304
00:12:58,700 --> 00:12:59,700
Got it!

305
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:00,700
Let us break.

306
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:01,700
Left side!

307
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:02,700
Yeah!

308
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,700
Vushuaka!

309
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:10,700
Three man block!

310
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:14,700
Wow!

311
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:17,700
Karasuno's Libero is nailing those receives every time now!

312
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:20,700
I'll be impressed once Vushuaka's playing up to his full potential.

313
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:22,700
You think you could take him on?

314
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:23,700
Yeah, but I don't feel like it.

315
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:24,700
Damn!

316
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:25,700
Sorry!

317
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:26,700
It was too close for the net!

318
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:27,700
Yeah!

319
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:28,700
Good job!

320
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:29,700
Don't give up!

321
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:30,700
We're so close!

322
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:31,700
Send it, Shirabu!

323
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,700
I got it!

324
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:33,700
Nice receipt!

325
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:34,700
Right side!

326
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:35,700
Yeah!

327
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:36,700
Nice guy, Jin!

328
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,700
Yeah!

329
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,700
Nice guy, Jin!

330
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:51,700
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

331
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:55,540
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

332
00:13:55,540 --> 00:14:00,620
You know there's no way I'll be able to beat Vushuwaka.

333
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:08,620
It's just that our bodies, experience levels, and time we've devoted to the sport are very different.

334
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:13,660
There's just no way I can beat him.

335
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:28,240
I was hoping we'd be able to break through while we still had Hinata as a decoy.

336
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:31,580
Take a look at how anxious Hinata is in the back row.

337
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:35,440
I don't blame him, though. Both his serves and digs kind of suck.

338
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:50,280
If their number 5's guest blocks could score either 120 points or 0 points,

339
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:53,980
then my read blocks ought to safely net me around 75.

340
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:03,480
Although, I admit our blocking technique is a bit amateur compared to the guest blocks.

341
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:08,400
But I still like our odds, even if the audience prefers the more showy ones.

342
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:16,040
I absolutely won't let their setter get any sense of satisfaction or accomplishment from overcoming our blocks.

343
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:25,480
Persistently, tenaciously, nimbly, and absolutely...

344
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:29,140
I will not let them through.

345
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:29,600
Damn.

346
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:34,520
I'm going to continue layering the stress and pressure on them.

347
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:35,400
One touch!

348
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,720
Get it!

349
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:42,520
Cut that!

350
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:46,920
Get it!

351
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:51,780
Good serve! I got it!

352
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:54,780
Your serves suck.

353
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:56,400
Your receives suck.

354
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:58,900
Even your setups and blocks are below average.

355
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:01,120
So why are you on the court?

356
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:05,000
To score points!

357
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:12,720
It's a break!

358
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:14,380
Amazing.

359
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:14,960
Awesome, Hinata!

360
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:18,740
The back attack at minus tempo has gotten even faster since Oikawa stopped it.

361
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:19,480
Taiji!

362
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:21,420
You gotta go for the ball!

363
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,320
Oh, whatever.

364
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:23,860
That was totally unblockable.

365
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,180
Nice one touch.

366
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:25,880
One more!

367
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:30,200
Yeah, but if Hinata hadn't come in and covered me, it would have just gotten blown away.

368
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:32,460
Nah, give yourself some credit.

369
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,260
It took that one touch to get it rolling in the first place.

370
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:39,180
Ishiro-bu.

371
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:42,620
Direct them to me.

372
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:47,580
Oh, crap!

373
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,300
It's going out.

374
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:51,080
I think.

375
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:53,660
If I guess wrong, I'll be the reason we lose.

376
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:56,100
It went off course.

377
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:57,340
It was going in?

378
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:57,940
I'm sorry!

379
00:16:58,280 --> 00:16:58,720
Ushiwaka!

380
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,000
Alright, we've got three blockers.

381
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:03,000
And...

382
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:03,200
Jump!

383
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:20,680
That was really intense.

384
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:24,220
It was like the game's momentum changed in a single hit.

385
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,240
Don't let them pull ahead.

386
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:28,240
Let's try again.

387
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:28,680
Yeah!

388
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:28,780
Yeah!

389
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:38,420
Oh, damn, he's good.

390
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:47,140
Synchronized attack!

391
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:54,460
If we could just keep scoring points, there's no way we could lose.

392
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:55,060
Yeah!

393
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:55,320
Yeah!

394
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,100
Taichi, you got this!

395
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:08,700
Ushiwaka!

396
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,000
And...

397
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:12,180
Jump!

398
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,540
Miss it!

399
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:19,360
Return it!

400
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:19,980
Return it!

401
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:33,420
We just have to open a path for our spiker.

402
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:40,680
This is exactly what I was waiting for.

403
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:43,980
A slight mistake created by...

404
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:45,760
Annoyance and panic.

405
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:57,300
...

406
00:18:57,300 --> 00:19:06,880
...

407
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:10,000
...

408
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,280
...

409
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:21,480
There's just no way I could beat him.

410
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,760
I'm just...

411
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:29,820
I'm just hoping that I can stop a few of his spikes.

412
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:34,780
Who is he? Who knows?

413
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:35,960
It's amazing!

414
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,460
Karasuno took the second setback!

415
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:40,500
Karasuno took the second setback!

416
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:43,700
This was just one block.

417
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:46,400
Just one point out of 25.

418
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:50,140
And this is just a high school team.

419
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:54,740
If that moment ever does come to you,

420
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:59,140
that's the moment you'll fall in love with volleyball.

421
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:10,940
There wasn't any weakness in Ushiwaka's spike just now.

422
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:22,740
His run and jump were also in perfect form here.

423
00:20:22,740 --> 00:20:27,180
If anything, that set was a little low, and maybe a little too close to the net.

424
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:33,040
I can't tell if Tsukishima honed in on that also, or if he's been patiently waiting for that exact chance.

425
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:38,900
At this time, I'd like to apologize for saying we couldn't stop it with blocks.

426
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:39,800
Clearly, I was wrong.

427
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:40,200
Huh?

428
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:44,380
And I do feel kind of bad because you look so concerned after I said it.

429
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,000
Huh?

430
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:49,800
Uh, well, I just honestly believed we were in good hands because of Tsuki's hard work.

431
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:53,860
I know it seems kind of out of character for him, but he hates losing.

432
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:56,480
So I knew he would pull something together in the end.

433
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:57,960
Tsukishima!

434
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,380
Nice block, champ!

435
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:00,840
That block was awesome!

436
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:10,460
I'm sure they faced blockers of my level, but they didn't account for factors like Nishinoya's receives and the weirdo duo's quick attacks.

437
00:21:10,460 --> 00:21:13,960
I knew those elements would put a lot of pressure on their setter.

438
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:19,080
You were really taking all those things into consideration?

439
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:21,040
Whoa, you got real issues, man.

440
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:27,640
If I know my brother, he was patiently waiting for that exact moment when Shira Torizawa would choke under pressure.

441
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:31,980
Wow, he waited a long time, but the payoff was sure worth it.

442
00:21:32,700 --> 00:21:34,140
Tsukishima is really smart.

443
00:21:34,540 --> 00:21:40,760
He has always struck me as the type of person who is always thinking and problem solving, whether it's in volleyball or in real life.

444
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:43,520
Sorry, I know he can spend a lot of time in his head.

445
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:44,500
No, not at all!

446
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:52,660
As I watched the game from above, I got the overwhelming feeling that the only thing on Tsukishima's mind was stopping that spike!

447
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:58,220
It makes me think that this is what it must be like for him when he solves a difficult problem on a test!

448
00:22:03,520 --> 00:22:04,000
Tsukishima!

449
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,680
At one point was worth a hundred!

450
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:09,880
Good job!

451
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:15,660
Thank you!

452
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:15,740
Thank you!

453
00:22:19,740 --> 00:22:20,140
Hey!

454
00:22:20,620 --> 00:22:21,380
What's the-

455
00:22:21,380 --> 00:22:22,580
Simmer down now, Hinata!

456
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:26,640
I know he's incapable of displaying any form of emotion, but he's now our beloved MVP!

457
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:29,700
Please, stop making a fuss.

458
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:30,320
Huh?

459
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:33,200
It was just one point.

460
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:37,340
The real battle begins now.

461
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:38,600
Yeah!

462
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:38,680
Yeah!

463
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,440
力すくじゃまだ届かずしまい

464
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:47,600
ギリギリで繋いで放つ願い

465
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:49,980
ただ、人やタイミングには恵まれて

466
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:52,820
へこたれずにいられてる

467
00:22:52,820 --> 00:22:54,900
真っ向から勝負したい

468
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:57,180
迷ってもじっとこらえとこう

469
00:22:57,180 --> 00:23:00,120
チャンスはそこにある

470
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:05,340
Oh、後は君次第です

471
00:23:05,340 --> 00:23:10,120
うん、後は君次第

472
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:13,760
ひとりそう願いを叶えるもん

473
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:16,400
黙って明日を迎えるもん

474
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:19,260
後は君次第

475
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:22,920
今はゆとりもないし

476
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,380
悟るには早い

477
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:29,160
風の色目に染みる

478
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:31,040
ゆとり思って

479
00:23:31,040 --> 00:23:33,460
サトリ脂め込んで

480
00:23:33,460 --> 00:23:38,580
ココリ高く生きたい

481
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:39,780
No doubt

482
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:42,660
RIVER 後は君次第

483
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:43,080
です

484
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:47,120
うん、全部君次第

485
00:23:47,120 --> 00:24:15,500
All right, Suki finally stopped Ushiwaka.

486
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:21,480
That's my bro. He makes me so proud. He might be blunt at times to keep to himself, but he's such a good egg, he's just trying to live his best life.

487
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:22,880
What, are you his mom or something?

488
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:25,840
Next, Haikyuu, one versus many.

